WEBVTT

00:27.260 --> 00:30.220
Be careful. He's strong.

00:30.700 --> 00:31.600
Got it.

00:33.350 --> 00:37.090
Wh-What's going on? It's still so early.

00:41.830 --> 00:45.070
He doesn't seem to be here.

00:45.470 --> 00:47.950
There's so much crap, it's hard to tell.

00:49.100 --> 00:50.960
Throw it all out.

00:54.430 --> 00:57.230
What the hell are they doing?

00:59.390 --> 01:00.490
He escaped.

01:01.330 --> 01:02.030
What?

01:02.530 --> 01:04.050
Gardar escaped.

01:04.600 --> 01:08.300
What other reason would
they have to search our shed?

01:14.760 --> 01:15.990
Arnheid!

03:09.420 --> 03:13.710
Great Purpose

03:18.490 --> 03:20.010
Wait, Einar!

03:20.890 --> 03:24.390
Stop, Einar!

03:25.200 --> 03:29.500
If Gardar escaped,
he'll look for Arnheid again.

03:31.980 --> 03:34.250
What will you accomplish by going to Arnheid?

03:34.950 --> 03:37.020
Will you drive back Gardar?

03:40.520 --> 03:43.600
I don't know, but...

03:45.400 --> 03:51.260
There must be something I can do for Arnheid.

04:14.430 --> 04:15.760
Arnheid!

04:21.850 --> 04:23.620
It's not him.

04:23.620 --> 04:27.050
It's not Gardar. Just two slaves.

04:28.310 --> 04:31.620
What are their names again?

04:31.620 --> 04:34.130
You mean the master's slaves.

04:35.260 --> 04:37.600
Thorfinn and Einar, huh?

04:38.010 --> 04:40.100
Yeah, those guys.

04:40.100 --> 04:42.110
What are they doing here?

04:43.460 --> 04:46.390
What should we do, boss?
Should we chase them off?

04:48.330 --> 04:52.860
No, leave them alone.
Let them do what they want.

05:05.400 --> 05:08.650
Um, Arnheid...

05:11.270 --> 05:15.410
Yes. You're here about Gardar.

05:17.100 --> 05:18.800
You know?

05:22.620 --> 05:23.410
Yes.

05:26.110 --> 05:29.820
I helped him escape.

05:31.400 --> 05:34.830
I cut the ropes binding him.

05:38.840 --> 05:42.530
Gardar, he... the man watching him....

05:43.030 --> 05:51.570
I thought we'd both be killed, so I...

06:00.010 --> 06:10.010
Then Gardar killed all the other guests
who came to see what was happening.

06:16.940 --> 06:18.570
More dead guests...

06:19.090 --> 06:21.770
The situation couldn't be worse.

06:27.130 --> 06:28.050
Einar...

06:28.990 --> 06:31.090
We're being watched by guests.

06:31.090 --> 06:34.970
Kneel next to Arnheid and
pretend to wash dishes.

06:42.360 --> 06:46.410
Stay calm, and tell us what's happening.

06:49.960 --> 06:55.500
Gardar was badly injured in the f-fight.

06:56.840 --> 07:03.790
We fled here in the rain,
to the old master's house.

07:05.530 --> 07:11.530
But Gardar lost consciousness
while I was tending his wounds.

07:12.600 --> 07:15.120
He was too heavy to carry.

07:15.750 --> 07:20.050
I was barely able to hide him.

07:21.630 --> 07:24.400
So Gardar is here.

07:24.990 --> 07:30.430
Yes. The old master helped me.

07:31.030 --> 07:34.720
Snake and his men arrived soon after.

07:36.330 --> 07:43.500
They seem to think Gardar fled
and is hiding somewhere.

07:45.350 --> 07:51.210
They're waiting for Gardar
to come for me at the house.

07:51.640 --> 07:54.970
Mister Snake and two other men are inside.

07:58.120 --> 08:02.710
Why... Why would you do something
so reckless by yourself?

08:03.400 --> 08:07.730
And after you said we'd wait out the storm
for the sake of the child inside you.

08:15.630 --> 08:17.930
Why?

08:27.710 --> 08:29.120
Perhaps...

08:30.680 --> 08:35.020
Perhaps I was dreaming.

08:35.910 --> 08:42.650
Dreaming of a life as part of a family
with Gardar and the child inside me.

08:44.380 --> 08:49.470
I thought that perhaps he had returned...

08:53.030 --> 08:57.170
I thought he'd returned.

09:02.840 --> 09:11.040
Those eyes that used to be
so full of confidence...

09:17.080 --> 09:19.870
They looked so miserable.

09:22.680 --> 09:30.290
We've lived so miserably
since we lost Hjalti.

09:33.550 --> 09:37.970
But I still dream...

09:50.990 --> 09:55.450
How are Gardar's injuries?
Has the bleeding stopped?

10:00.710 --> 10:05.120
He was bleeding badly
from the right side of his chest.

10:06.190 --> 10:10.700
He was still bleeding when I hid him.

10:13.080 --> 10:15.210
Every moment counts.

10:23.910 --> 10:25.130
Arnheid...

10:27.080 --> 10:32.320
Are you prepared to cast your lot with Gardar?

10:42.090 --> 10:47.370
If you want to live with Gardar,
then you'll have to flee together.

10:49.640 --> 10:51.900
But you're pregnant.

10:52.680 --> 10:55.180
The road ahead will be difficult.

10:56.940 --> 10:59.040
But if you still want to try,

11:00.650 --> 11:02.590
then I will help you.

11:04.570 --> 11:07.930
It's the only option left.

11:18.330 --> 11:22.080
The only option, huh?

11:26.120 --> 11:28.850
I'll help, too.

11:28.850 --> 11:32.160
Together, we may be able to do something.

11:33.630 --> 11:34.780
Thorfinn...

11:52.770 --> 11:54.780
Ow! What—

11:55.120 --> 11:56.470
Don't sleep.

11:56.470 --> 12:00.450
If you take your eyes off Arnheid again,
I'll break your nose.

12:00.910 --> 12:03.580
Y-Yes, boss. Sorry.

12:08.650 --> 12:09.520
Who's there?

12:11.790 --> 12:15.740
I'd like to begin preparing lunch.

12:18.920 --> 12:21.700
Take the tools you need and cook in the yard.

12:21.700 --> 12:25.570
You're the bait.
Stay where you'll be seen.

12:27.660 --> 12:30.370
Very well. I understand.

12:41.350 --> 12:44.910
What a pitiful bunch.

12:45.740 --> 12:47.820
Right, Snake?

12:51.150 --> 12:58.690
They say inferior people
can't help but become slaves.

12:59.450 --> 13:01.900
That it's where they belong.

13:03.070 --> 13:06.270
But I don't think so.

13:06.720 --> 13:12.220
Slaves were just unlucky. That's all.

13:13.190 --> 13:19.310
If you and I had been unlucky,
we might've ended up as slaves, too.

13:20.350 --> 13:24.570
So what? That's got nothing to do with this.

13:24.990 --> 13:27.340
He killed five of my men.

13:27.690 --> 13:30.540
I won't be satisfied until he's dead.

13:32.090 --> 13:35.400
I can't walk around wearing this sword

13:35.400 --> 13:38.510
when I'm crying myself to sleep
over my unavenged men.

13:43.150 --> 13:46.340
Then throw away your sword.

13:50.910 --> 13:56.860
Even I can tell that sword
isn't from around here.

13:57.320 --> 14:01.970
There was a reason you ended up here.

14:03.000 --> 14:09.180
But I doubt throwing away your sword
would allow you to escape whatever it was.

14:10.920 --> 14:15.650
Enough talking, Gramps.
It's time for your nap.

14:18.470 --> 14:21.390
You can have my farm.

14:22.310 --> 14:26.870
Work the land. Produce life.

14:26.870 --> 14:30.510
That's better than swinging around a sword.

14:34.110 --> 14:40.650
I can no longer stand and walk.
Soon I will die.

14:41.350 --> 14:45.310
It's a good opportunity for you
to straighten out your life.

14:47.900 --> 14:53.390
I owe you for reading the Bible to me.

14:57.050 --> 15:00.770
Don't talk about that nonsense now.

15:00.770 --> 15:02.770
I'm not doing no stinking field work.

15:04.760 --> 15:05.760
Boss.

15:05.760 --> 15:06.490
Huh?

15:06.840 --> 15:08.720
There's someone out there.

15:12.200 --> 15:15.350
Over there. Third tree from the back.

15:16.430 --> 15:19.480
That's probably him in its shadow.

15:23.020 --> 15:24.530
All right.

15:56.730 --> 15:57.770
They're coming out.

15:58.230 --> 16:01.290
One, two, three...

16:01.770 --> 16:03.480
That's all of them.

16:07.990 --> 16:10.560
I'm counting on you, Einar.

16:28.130 --> 16:29.620
Spread out.

16:30.050 --> 16:32.890
We'll follow him from different
positions and vantages.

16:37.950 --> 16:42.770
Sir, I'm sorry, but I need to
borrow your horse and cart.

16:42.770 --> 16:46.430
I promise I'll pay you back
by working for you.

16:47.350 --> 16:49.810
Don't worry about that.

16:49.810 --> 16:53.190
More importantly, load me into the cart.

16:53.190 --> 16:58.160
If I'm there, we'll be able to travel
around the farm unquestioned.

16:58.160 --> 17:02.570
But we can't involve you in this...

17:03.720 --> 17:06.420
I'm already involved.

17:06.910 --> 17:10.670
Now quit arguing and help me.

17:11.580 --> 17:14.960
Y-Yes, sir. Thank you.

17:19.930 --> 17:21.410
Damn that Gardar...

17:21.810 --> 17:23.710
He's trying to flee into the woods.

17:24.310 --> 17:27.450
We won't be able to use
the horses in the woods.

17:27.450 --> 17:29.900
Catch him. Don't let him enter the woods.

17:33.990 --> 17:36.330
Damn it! It's so far away...

17:53.630 --> 17:56.770
He's alive. His wounds were treated well.

17:58.040 --> 18:00.700
But he's as cold as a stone.

18:01.670 --> 18:03.490
He lost too much blood.

18:05.000 --> 18:07.470
Please hang in there.

18:12.750 --> 18:13.990
He's fast.

18:14.650 --> 18:18.850
A gravely injured man
could never run that fast.

18:20.360 --> 18:22.580
Spider! Badger!

18:22.580 --> 18:24.480
Stay on him.

18:25.000 --> 18:27.110
Don't force a confrontation.

18:27.110 --> 18:31.340
If that's Gardar, you won't
stand a chance against him.

18:31.950 --> 18:34.070
I'll send reinforcements later.

18:34.070 --> 18:36.190
Keep following him until then.

18:36.630 --> 18:38.090
You got that?

18:38.430 --> 18:39.710
I'm counting on you guys.

18:40.600 --> 18:43.600
What? Wait, where are you going, boss?

18:46.920 --> 18:49.090
The cart is ready.

18:49.090 --> 18:51.360
We'll hurry toward the border to the south.

18:51.860 --> 18:55.910
Once you're out of the country, it'll be
difficult for the guests to pursue you.

18:56.630 --> 18:59.110
I'll leave you partway to distract them.

18:59.110 --> 19:01.260
I'll draw as many pursuers to me as I can.

19:02.840 --> 19:06.960
Sir, could you accompany them
to the edge of the farm?

19:07.270 --> 19:09.760
Got it.

19:42.010 --> 19:44.300
I didn't hear horses.

19:47.910 --> 19:50.300
Did he dismount and run here?

19:56.230 --> 19:57.630
I see.

19:58.800 --> 20:01.810
So he's unconscious.

20:02.590 --> 20:05.580
No wonder I couldn't sense him.

20:12.360 --> 20:13.610
Thorfinn...

20:25.080 --> 20:29.710
Just so you know, Thorfinn,
I'm not here to negotiate.

20:32.120 --> 20:34.610
Hand over Gardar.

20:35.580 --> 20:37.120
Otherwise,

20:38.350 --> 20:39.450
I'll kill you.

20:46.520 --> 20:48.050
There were three pursuers.

20:48.590 --> 20:51.020
But only Snake is here.

20:51.020 --> 20:52.610
I don't sense the others.

20:53.550 --> 20:58.190
If I can subdue him somehow,
we can still escape.

20:59.610 --> 21:03.530
I'll slip past his sword and
deal a single blow to his chin.

21:06.780 --> 21:09.280
You gonna fight him, Thorfinn?

21:09.280 --> 21:12.640
Good grief. I guess
you can't help it this time.

21:13.040 --> 21:15.590
You're helping someone.

21:15.590 --> 21:18.930
You've got a good reason to raise your fists.

21:21.260 --> 21:23.550
But, you know,

21:23.910 --> 21:27.870
I'm sure he's got a good reason, too.

21:28.930 --> 21:31.150
What will you do, Thorfinn?

21:31.570 --> 21:39.200
Will you remain a pacifist, or will you
fight him in order to help someone else?

21:41.940 --> 21:45.840
Which road leads to becoming a true warrior?

21:46.390 --> 21:48.860
There's no time to think about it.

21:50.450 --> 21:53.210
Look. He's right in front of you.

22:57.400 --> 23:00.210
Do you think you can beat him
while you're still half-asleep?

23:32.350 --> 23:34.060
That's an odd stance.

23:34.790 --> 23:36.810
Not right for a spear or an ax...

23:37.580 --> 23:38.540
A sword?

23:41.600 --> 23:42.640
No...

25:37.050 --> 25:39.970
The Road Home

25:38.280 --> 25:39.420
"The Road Home."
